{
  "bridge_text": "寒风依旧在田野间呼啸，莉娜的红外套在雪地里像一点微弱的火光。她没有回头，坚定地走向那棵发出低鸣的古树。",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "text": "每当冬夜降临，树皮深处总会传出阵阵低鸣，大人们总是告诫孩子们离那儿远点。可自从奶奶没讲完那个故事就睡着了，莉娜心里便像长了草一样。她穿上那件暖和的红毛衣外套，踩着厚厚的积雪，独自走向了那棵古树。"
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s1"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "While the fox holds his secrets close, his heavy heart seems to weigh down the very air around him. Lina steps forward, determined to show him that kindness can find a way where grumpiness cannot.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Lina looked at the stern fox, his grey fur ruffled and his eyes darting toward the darkness below. She knew he wanted her to leave, but she could not turn back when the mystery of the humming felt so close. She took a breath, holding her ground as the leaves whispered against the bark."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk pointed a shaky claw at the door, his jaw set in a line of stubborn silence. Lina reached into her pocket and pulled out the last apple of the season, round and crisp. She set it on the step between them and whispered that it was for the trouble of walking her down. Mosk stared at the fruit for a long time, his whiskers twitching, before he stood up and stepped onto the first stair without a word."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "Mosk the fox certainly has a heart as tangled as those old tree roots. With the apple offered and the grumpy guardian moving aside, the path ahead finally opens.",
  "resume_strategy": "skip",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Lina reached into her pocket and pulled out the last apple of the season. She set it on the step between them, offering it as a small peace token for the trouble of her visit. Mosk stared at the crisp red fruit for a long time. Then, his grumpiness softening just a fraction, he stood up, straightened his patched vest, and stepped onto the first stair to lead the way down."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "At the bottom of the stairs, the humming revealed itself as a quiet, rhythmic song. A firefly, large as a robin, lay resting on a bed of moss, her golden glow dimming to a flicker. Mosk’s whiskers trembled as he looked at her. He whispered that she had been his dearest friend, but he had failed to bring her medicine one winter long ago. He had been guarding this hollow tree ever since, too ashamed to face the light he had let grow cold."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s3"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "While sneaking might feel safer, Lina knows that kindness often unlocks doors that force cannot touch. With that apple resting on the step, Mosk finally finds the courage to move.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk stared at the apple for a long time, his sharp eyes softening just a fraction. Then he stood up, pulled his vest tight against the draft, and stepped onto the first stair without a word. He seemed to carry the weight of the forest in his heavy, rhythmic tread as he led the way down."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s3"
