{
  "bridge_text": "Just like a fuzzy blanket for the forest floor, the moss cradled the fading firefly in the dim light. The sad memory of that long-ago winter hung heavy in the air as Mosk stood trembling before his old friend.",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "At the bottom of the stairs, the humming was a quiet song, and a firefly the size of a robin lay on a bed of soft, velvet-green moss. Her glow was almost out. Mosk’s whiskers trembled as he looked at the mossy bed, remembering the winter he failed to bring her medicine. He had been guarding the tree ever since, too ashamed to face the friend he had once let down."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s4"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "With old Mosk watching her from his perch on the stairs, Lina decided that her curiosity was far stronger than his warnings. She looked at the fox and prepared to make her move.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Lina stood her ground, looking up at the old fox. She told him firmly that she could not possibly forget a sound she had not yet heard. Mosk, his fur bristling, narrowed his eyes at her as if deciding whether to let her pass or send her back into the forest."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "Just as the numbers in the world grow large and complex, so too do the secrets of the woods. With the apple placed as a peace offering, Mosk finally begins his descent into the shadows.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
