{
  "bridge_text": "The shadows hold their breath just as we do, waiting to see if that tiny light will return. With the firefly resting on her mossy bed, Lina stepped forward to see if she could help.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "Mosk's whiskers trembled as he remembered that winter long ago when he failed to bring her medicine. He had been guarding the tree ever since, too ashamed to face her, but now he stood frozen in the dim, pulsing light. Her glow was almost out, flickering like a dying ember in the dark, and the quiet song of the tree seemed to hold its breath."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "text": "Lina knelt beside the moss, gently asking the firefly queen what she needed to feel strong again. A drop of warm milk and a kind word, the queen whispered, for that was all medicine had ever truly been. Mosk carefully fetched the milk in a silver thimble, laying his large, weary paw beside hers. As the queen’s glow steadied, the tree’s humming bloomed into a song Lina had never heard before, and Mosk hummed along."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s4"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "The path ahead holds many secrets, but we shall reach the end soon enough. For now, let us see what waits for Lina at the base of those hollow stairs.",
  "resume_strategy": "skip",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Inside the hollow tree she found a curl of stairs going down, and at the very top step sat an old grey fox in a patched green vest. His name was Mosk. He told her, in a voice like dry leaves, that the tree was not for visiting and that she should go home and forget the humming. Lina stood tall, her eyes bright, and told him she could not forget a song she had not yet heard."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
